-- title:
--   Ends of the blow-up chart are incomparable
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q \ge 5$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Further, $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and the hypothesis `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$.
--
--   The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` identifies it with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of the modular curve of level $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup $H = \ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   The base is a discrete valuation ring $A$, a domain with fraction field $L$, henselian local with algebraically closed residue field, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; the residue characteristic is $q$ in the sense that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`), and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). The element $j \in K$ has Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ of the classical $q$-expansion $t^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } j_{\mathrm{Num}})$ of the modular $j$-function, and $j \ne 0$. A uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ is fixed by `hϖ`, and `hϖt` provides $\varpi_t \in A$ together with a unit $u$ of $A$ satisfying $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = qu$.
--
--   The chart algebra $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` consists of the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, with $j$ itself denoted `jChartFin A (↥K) j`; [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the scheme obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and the corresponding chart for $j^{-1}$, with structural morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with $\operatorname{Spec} C =$ `XFin` embedded by `ιFin`. The ideal $y \subseteq C$ is maximal and contains the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and the hypothesis `hss` expresses that $y$ is supersingular: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is a rigidity statement about the formal completion at supersingular points of the integral model. It asserts: for every point $z$ of the two-chart model, with $\varpi_z$ the germ at $z$ of the global image of $\varpi$ and $\varpi_z \in \mathfrak{m}$ of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin`-image $z$ whose $j$-invariant is supersingular in the sense above, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ (a domain, adically complete for $\mathfrak{m}_W$), a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion $\mathrm{CMP}$ of the stalk $\mathrm{STK}$ at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u\bigr)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC} : \mathrm{STK} \to \mathrm{CMP}$, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map and $\mathrm{germY} : C \to \mathrm{STK}$ for the germ map at $z$ through $y'$, the following seven clauses hold: (1) $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}))$ carries the image of each $a \in A$ to $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma a))$; (2) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on the group attached to $(N_0, H)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g \neq 0$, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and all embeddings $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i /(q\ell)}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}_{q\ell}(\gamma^{-1})$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}_{q\ell}(\gamma^{-1})$ — such $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; (3) if moreover $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (4) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with the action of $\tau$ on $C$; $\theta$ fixing every constant $\mathrm{mkS}(C(w))$; $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_j)) \equiv \sum_i \mathrm{mkS}(C(M_{ij})X_i)$ modulo the square of $(\mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1))$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$; and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (5) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$ but not both $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, and each containing an element of the shape $\mathrm{mkS}(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct as soon as $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ satisfying the same two conditions and containing an element $\mathrm{mkS}(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (7) the function $j_{q\ell} :=$ [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-expansion with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with $j_{q\ell} - a_0 \in y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is anisotropic in the sense that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i, e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$ for all $a, b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, such that $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(j_{q\ell} - a_0))) = \mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   A particular such situation is then fixed: a point $z$ with $\varpi_z$, `hϖz`, `hz` as above, a point $y'$ of `XFin` over $z$ with supersingular $j$-invariant (`hss'`) and $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`), together with data $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1$ (with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv$ `drinfeldForm q W₁` modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$) and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this fixed data precisely the seven clauses (1)–(7) listed above.
--
--   The ideal $J \subseteq C$ is prescribed by `hJ` as the infimum, over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, of the contraction along the induced endomorphism of $C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal $(\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)), \mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1))$ of $S$. The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ is prescribed by `hB` as the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, viewed as an $A$-subalgebra; $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The remaining hypotheses on this blow-up chart are: `hR1`, that $C \subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \ne 0$; `hR2`, that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ if and only if it lies in $W$ with image in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the set of ratios $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k_A`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $= k_A[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}_q - 1)$ with kernel the centre $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, compatible with $A \to k_A$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserve $W$, via an element $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}_q\gamma, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)c^{q+1}$) acting through `hAction`, with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that such $\tau$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is obtained from the centre by some $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ after every such $\tau$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally, $O$ and $O'$ are subrings of $K$, each assumed (in `hO`, respectively `hO'`) to be an end of the blow-up: there are $a \in J$ with $a \ne 0$ in $K$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a := C[\{x \in K : xa \in J\}]$ (viewed as an $A$-subalgebra) such that the ring in question is the set of ratios $g/h$ with $g, h \in B_a$ and $h \notin P$, every element of $y$ lying in that ring is a non-unit there, and $B$ is not contained in it. The hypothesis `hle` is that $O' \subseteq O$.
--
--   The conclusion is the single equality $O = O'$.
--
--   This is the separatedness input for the blow-up of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ along the centre $J$ at a supersingular point, phrased on two affine charts without constructing the blow-up as a scheme: the local rings of distinct ends are pairwise incomparable, so an end contained in another end coincides with it. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.end_blowupChart_eq_of_on_same_component_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.end_blowupChart_eq_of_on_same_component_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_not_isUnit_isUnit_of_isEnd_blowupChart_ne_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_not_isUnit_isUnit_of_isEnd_blowupChart_ne_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), which produces a function vanishing at one end and invertible at another.
